:pack   Treasure Trash — sketches (not in the game)
:format 1
;
; legend  # wall  - floor  @ raccoon  $ bag  C full can  c empty can
;         x spilled trash  E exit  + raccoon on exit  b recycle bin
;         W wheelie bin (full)  w wheelie bin (empty)
;
; These six were the old L8-L13: a difficulty ladder FOUND by a seeded generator, not
; composed. They verify — every par here is provably minimal — but metrics.mjs showed
; the ladder is built out of walking rather than decisions (par climbs 15 -> 25 while
; board-changing decisions stay flat at 3-5), so they are out of the game pack.
;
; Kept because they are green and because the rooms that replace them have to beat
; something. Verify with:  node verify.mjs levels/sketches.tt levels/sketches.sol
;

:level  S1
:name   Bin Night
:teach  both containers at once — the can that ejects a bag and the bin that drops trash
:par    15
:traps  7
:solves 1
:solve  lDldL!rurrdLLdR!l
:note   The can hands you a second bag to deal with and the bin charges you a cell of floor. Neither can be left where it stands.
:grid
-b--@
---C-
-$---
--E--
-----
-----
:end

:level  S2
:name   Tight Corner
:teach  the exit wedged between two bags and the bin that can bury the way through
:par    17
:traps  3
:solves 2
:solve  uruullDurrddD!ulU!d
:note   Only three ways to lose this one, and all of them are the same mistake: filling the gap you have to come back through.
:grid
------
------
b$----
-E----
-@$---
------
:end

:level  S3
:name   Long Way Round
:teach  the wheelie bin again, now with the walk home as part of the cost
:par    19
:traps  16
:solves 1
:solve  uuulDdddlU!drrddLuL!r
:note   The bin rolls away from the exit, so freeing the bag and reaching the door pull in opposite directions.
:grid
-----
---W-
--$--
----@
----E
-----
:end

:level  S4
:name   Crosstown
:teach  two bags on opposite corners with one rolling bin between them
:par    21
:traps  34
:solves 1
:solve  rrUuurD!ulluuRdR!lulD!ul
:note   The bin is the only piece that crosses the board, and it only crosses once per shove.
:grid
E-----
-$----
------
---W$-
-@----
------
:end

:level  S5
:name   The Far Side
:teach  a bag and a bin parked as far from the exit as the room allows
:par    23
:traps  12
:solves 3
:solve  uuuurrDdL!rddrddLuL!ruuuu
:note   Nothing here is subtle. The room is long because the pieces are far apart and the bin will not stop where you want it.
:grid
----E-
--$W--
------
------
-@----
------
:end

:level  S6
:name   Closing Time
:teach  everything the pack has taught, at the longest range it has asked for
:par    25
:traps  43
:solves 2
:solve  uuuulDddlU!ddddRrU!dlllluR!l
:note   Two bags, a rolling bin, and an exit on the far wall. The last room in the pack and the only one that needs all of it at once.
:grid
------
---$W-
------
------
E$---@
------
:end
